  "notes": "Cash Money and No Limit, built on the Triggerman/Brown Beat cell. ⛔ **The one parameter that separates this from `crunk` is `halfTime: false`.** Crunk is a half-time kit with the clap on 3 at 135–160; this is a straight backbeat on 2 and 4 at 92–105, and every other difference follows from that. The fixed rhythm cell is the snare *answer*: `snare.placement` is `backbeat_24` and `snare.offSnare` puts a second snare voice on the \"&\" of 2 at prob 0.85 — that answer is the grammar, not a variation on it. There is deliberately **no `layerClapOffsetMs`**: crunk's signature is a huge layered clap and bounce's is a bare TR-808 snare, so the clap lane is absent rather than quiet. The standing 8th layer is `percs.tambourine: true` (a real steady-8ths stream, not a sprinkle) with cowbell, conga, tom and rim answering offbeat. Harmony is bright major/mixolydian, which nothing else in this family is: layered keyboards \"punctuate every song\", so `melody.emptyBarBias` is the lowest here (0.06) against crunk's 0.15 — crunk empties the bar for the chant, bounce fills it with keyboards. ⚠ **`bass808.role` is `counter_riff` rather than `bassline`, and that is a deliberate use of the engine's only lever for a genuine two-voice low end.** The research is explicit that the 808 sub is tuned to the key with a long decay *and* that Mannie played a Moog \"specifically for bass lines — the low end is played, not drawn\", and No Limit's bench is \"sustained 808 sub plus a synth-bass line playing roots and fifths in a funk rhythm\". `role: \"bassline\"` makes `bass::generate` return an empty lane, so the played bass would not exist at all. With `slideProb` at 0.06 the 808 stays a tuned pedal on the root, which is what the records do; `counter_riff` here means \"the 808 is not the whole bass\", not \"the 808 wanders\". The played line is `independent_riff` — not `mirror_kick`, which would land on the 808's own onsets and be one line played twice. ⚠ **INFERRED parameters, and this is why confidence is `medium` rather than `high`.** The research rates the *method* high (gear, sample abstinence, the beat-follows-vocal rule, the fill vocabulary, the tempo convention) and marks every numeric tempo band in the lane **[LOW-CONF]** — 92–105 straight is stated in the archetype recommendation and repeated as [LOW-CONF] on Juvenile, Mannie Fresh, B.G., Hot Boys and Choppa. Inferred rather than sourced: the key list, `swing` (kept straight at 0.50 because nothing in the research describes a shuffle and inventing one would be the loudest unsourced claim available), `humanize.quantizeStrength` at 0.86 — looser than crunk's 0.95, extrapolated from Mannie MIDI-ing electronic drum pads \"just to have that real drum feel\" and from the documented SP-12/808 tempo-matching drift — every velocity tier, every register, and the whole `intervals`/`contour` split. `chords.progressionFamilies` are inferred from \"major/mixolydian\", \"often one chord for the whole record\" and Big Tymers' \"I–IV or I–V–vi\"; the I-alone family carries the heaviest weight because a single chord is bounce's stated harmonic norm. ⚠ `chordDurationBeats` [2, 8] plus three `harmonicRhythm` values are what carry this model's chord variety against the 55-distinct floor, rather than progressions the lane does not play — the research says 2–4 bar loops, so what varies is how long the loop sits, not what it sits on. ⚠ `snareRoll.pitchWalk` is inherited, not authored: nothing in the research says how these producers pitch a roll. ⚠ **Three things the research asks for that this model cannot say.** (1) The 808 tom roll into the hook — `snareRoll` is the only roll engine and it is a snare, so `percs.lanes` carries a tom that gets sprinkled rather than rolled. (2) Hi-hat *triplets*, which the research calls half of the entire fill vocabulary: the roll vocabulary here is fixed to `\"16\"` by this batch's authoring band, so the triplet is carried by `hihat.base`, which reaches `\"8T\"` about a fifth of the time — a triplet hat stream rather than a triplet fill. `continuous` is false so the triplet grid is never cross-filled with 16ths, and `fillDensity` stays at 0.70–0.95 so every seed still gets hats. (3) The whistle as an instrumental element — there is no whistle lane and no whistle `timbreHint`; the `triggerman` mode uses `square_lead`, which is the nearest voice the dataset already names.",
